#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050765 :topic/difficulty 0.6027738609637455 :topic/id #uuid "64dbabd7-08e6-5435-b006-ab4997312f47" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059767 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059576 :question/id #uuid "b2196eb1-6691-549b-950a-a9bab6863a70" :question/math-academy-id "e-4683" :question/problem "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 2y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 0x+2y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n\t\t1 & -2  \\\\\n\t\t0 & 2 \n\t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb13e9d9-19f0-5f39-b9f8-e6e2f8fac433" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient Matrix of a System of Linear Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059768 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059577 :question/id #uuid "b5967dd6-bdf9-5cd0-9639-ec2816d04256" :question/math-academy-id "e-4684" :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+x-5-3z &=0 \\\\ z &=y+7x \\\\ y+3-2z &=1-2x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-3z &=5 \\\\ -7x-y+z &=0 \\\\ 2x+y-2z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n\t\t1 & 1 & -3  \\\\\n\t\t-7 & -1 & 1  \\\\\n                2 & 1 & -2 \n\t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f9ccaa5-d69c-584d-946e-0c57b3050160" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a System of Linear Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059769 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059578 :question/id #uuid "05942b5f-c165-59c6-8b67-24bc8dd40cca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4685" :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and $y,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-4y &=-12 \\\\ 3x+y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7c8f4da-c782-51e0-ac51-87a89f31860d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the System of Equations Associated With an Augmented Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059770 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059579 :question/id #uuid "161a4327-2356-5779-92a6-8495cfffefb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4686" :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{2} &=a \\\\ 5+3b-a &=4c \\\\ d &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c,d$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-a+0b+\\frac{1}{2}c+0d &=0 \\\\ -a+3b-4c+0d &=-5 \\\\ 0a+0b+0c+d &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14d047c8-f032-5ff3-aced-65d40bfeeaad" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a Linear System With Variables Other Than x, y, z"}] :topic/math-academy-id 148 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049120}] :topic/title "Systems of Equations as Augmented Matrices"}]}
